Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

CharacterFunctions::readDoubleValue accumulates the digits of an exponent into
an int with no bound, so a number like "1e99999999999" overflows a signed int:
undefined behaviour, reachable from a project file because every parameter
value is read with var -> double (found by tests/fuzz/fuzz_state with UBSan).
Stop accumulating at 100000; anything that large is out of double's range and
already becomes inf or 0 just below. Applied by CMakeLists.txt via
FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND.

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_core/text/juce_CharacterFunctions.h FLAYR_PATCH juce-double-exponent-overflow

diff --git a/modules/juce_core/text/juce_CharacterFunctions.h b/modules/juce_core/text/juce_CharacterFunctions.h
index 7a1edcd456..0cb319bfc1 100644
--- a/modules/juce_core/text/juce_CharacterFunctions.h
+++ b/modules/juce_core/text/juce_CharacterFunctions.h
@@ -373,7 +373,9 @@ public:
             {
                 auto digit = (int) text.getAndAdvance() - '0';
 
-                if (digit != 0 || exponent != 0)
+                // FLAYR_PATCH juce-double-exponent-overflow: stop accumulating once the exponent is out of double's range
+                // anyway; the unbounded version overflowed int (undefined behaviour).
+                if ((digit != 0 || exponent != 0) && exponent < 100000)
                     exponent = (exponent * 10) + digit;
             }
 
